                <pb facs="1243" n="1233" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1233"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Olive, William M.: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-15T18:00:00+08:00">July 15, 1949—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 15—7:29 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2789. At meeting of Consular body this morning regarding Olive case, British
                    Consul General stated that he had not had sufficient time consult Ambassador and
                    was therefore not prepared to discuss matter officially. It was finally agreed
                    that I should state case to Consular body and that each would thereafter be able
                    consult his Ambassador [and] Foreign Office if he felt it necessary. Further
                    discussion brought out a certain note of hesitancy among several consular
                    officers despite optimism expressed to me by Brazilian Consul who has been
                    particularly active. (I have naturally been careful to avoid any initiative with
                    colleagues as instructed by Dept.) Final decision was that consular body should
                    await result of our protest regarding Olive case and would then decide what next
                    step to take if any. In meantime, Consuls would have opportunity consult
                    respective authorities.</p>
                <p>Repeated Nanking 1571.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
